UCSD-P-System Licensing
=======================

UCSD-P-System combines several separately licensed works. Each one keeps its
original license, and the full license texts are in the files listed below.
Individual source files carry their own copyright and license notices, and
those notices take precedence over this summary.

Component                        License                       Full text
-------------------------------  ----------------------------  ----------------------------------
subprojects/ucsd-psystem-xc      GNU GPL v3 or later (*)       subprojects/ucsd-psystem-xc/LICENSE
subprojects/ucsd-psystem-fs      GNU GPL v3 or later (*)       subprojects/ucsd-psystem-fs/LICENSE
subprojects/ucsd-psystem-vm      GNU GPL v2 or later           subprojects/ucsd-psystem-vm/LICENSE
os (UCSD Pascal II.0 sources)    UCSD License 2.0              os/LICENSE-UCSD
os (ucsd-psystem-os additions)   BSD-style 3-clause            os/LICENSE
subprojects/libexplain,          GNU GPL v3 or later           subprojects/ucsd-psystem-xc/LICENSE
top-level build files

(*) Most of these files are licensed "GPL version 2 or later" and some are
    "GPL version 3 or later". The programs built from them are therefore
    distributed under GPL version 3 or later.


UCSD Pascal II.0
----------------

The p-System itself (compiler, editor, filer, operating system, and so on,
under os/) is:

    UCSD PASCAL - Version II.0
    Copyright (C) 1979 Regents of the University of California
    All Rights Reserved

The UCSD license allows use, copying, modification and distribution only for
educational, research and non-profit purposes. Commercial use requires a
separate agreement with the University of California, San Diego. See
os/LICENSE-UCSD for the complete terms.

The disk volumes produced by the build (system.vol, utility.vol,
diagnostic.vol) contain this code and are covered by the UCSD license.


